<title>USA: Glimcher Realty sells community center.</title>
<headline>Glimcher Realty sells community center.</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBUS, Ohio 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Glimcher Realty Trust said Monday it expects to post a profit of about $100,000 from the sale of a community center for $4.1 million.</p>
<p>Glimcher said it sold the Applewood Village community center in Fremont, Ohio. The sales price included the assumption of the center's $3.75 million mortgage and cash consideration of $350,000.</p>
<p>The property was acquired by Aufrecht-Grobman Enterprises, an Illinois general partnership.</p>
